grep searches for text.

#!/bin/bash

if grep -q "root" /etc/passwd; then
    echo "root user exists"
else
    echo "root user not found"
fi

-q means quiet mode.

It doesn't display the matching line. It only gives an exit status.

Linux Admin example

Check whether SSH is configured:

grep "PermitRootLogin" /etc/ssh/sshd_config
